ion in the z-axis has a translational offset.\n\n\nThe error stems from incorrectly defining the vector $\\mathbf{v}_3$ as always orthogonal ($v_{3x} = 0$).  This led to correct results for even periods because the x-component displacement became multiples of the in-plane lattice constant, aligning with the orthogonal cell. However, odd periods require a tilted translational vector for accurate representation, which the current implementation did not support.\n\n\nThe previous fix of orthogonalizing the lattice vector worked for even periods, but introduced an unphysical offset for odd periods due to the 2H-SiC lattice geometry. Correcting the script involves specifying the non-zero x-component of the third lattice vector, which introduces the required tilt to align the odd-period structure with the bulk calculation. The updated calculation with the corrected lattice vector now yields the expected four-fold coordinated structure, matching bond lengths and bulk energy precisely with the even-period result.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"rm -rf /tmp/test_odd_bulk\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Clean up temporary test directory\""}}]}
